  4.004317622227642*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ea8e962e-191c-404f-8f4d-\
a8c55c97d4ef"],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.004317604967182*^9, 
  4.004317609289034*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f6227816-01f2-444b-a85d-\
eb435bd7b32e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Analytic reference outputs (not represented as Mathematica kernel output)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7d8312d6-441e-aa42-bab5-79dcf8784b7e"],

Cell["\<\
For \[CapitalLambda] >> m, T(\[CapitalLambda]) = 1/(16\[Pi]\.b2)[\
\[CapitalLambda]\.b2 - m\.b2 ln(\[CapitalLambda]\.b2/m\.b2) - m\:2074/\
\[CapitalLambda]\.b2 + O(\[CapitalLambda]\:207b\:2074)] and B(0;\
\[CapitalLambda]) = 1/(16\[Pi]\.b2)[ln(\[CapitalLambda]\.b2/m\.b2) - 1 + 2m\
\.b2/\[CapitalLambda]\.b2 + O(\[CapitalLambda]\:207b\:2074)]. In DR, T = \
m\.b2/(16\[Pi]\.b2)[-2/\[CurlyEpsilon] + \[Gamma]_E - 1 - \
ln(4\[Pi]\[Mu]\.b2/m\.b2)] + O(\[CurlyEpsilon]), while B(0) = \
1/(16\[Pi]\.b2)[2/\[CurlyEpsilon] - \[Gamma]_E + ln(4\[Pi]\[Mu]\.b2/m\.b2)] + \
O(\[CurlyEpsilon]). The identity B(0) = -\[PartialD]T/\[PartialD]m\.b2 holds \
in both schemes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fa1cef35-5b78-8342-bacb-df07fa960fb2"],

Cell["\<\
The finite bubble difference is B(P)-B(0) = -(1/16\[Pi]\.b2)\[Integral]\:2080\
\.b9 dx ln[1+x(1-x)P\.b2/m\.b2], and its derivative at P\.b2=0 is -1/(96\[Pi]\
\.b2m\.b2). The sunset gamma ratio expands as \
-1/(2\[CurlyEpsilon])+\[Gamma]_E/2-13/8+O(\[CurlyEpsilon]). Including the \
full prefactor, its pole is -p\.b2/[2(4\[Pi])\:2074\[CurlyEpsilon]]. The \
derived critical expansion is \
\[Delta]=3+\[CurlyEpsilon]+25\[CurlyEpsilon]\.b2/54+O(\[CurlyEpsilon]\.b3), \
hence the \[CurlyEpsilon]=1 truncated estimate is 4.46296296296. From \
\[CapitalDelta]\[Sigma]=0.518148806, \[Eta]=0.036297612 and \
\[Delta]=4.78984254187.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6382780-d044-6a4f-8588-6ae8232ab263"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

