Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Textbook Anchor Map \[LongDash] FieldsI-Notes (Spring 2025)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"204e26cc-e2b4-d642-b1a7-236db9fa8db6"],

Cell["\<\
The companion file anchor_equation_map.md contains the full \
equation-by-equation map for Sections 1.1\[Dash]2.3. The following anchor IDs \
are the stable identifiers used throughout the project. References are to \
printed page numbers in FieldsI-Notes; unnumbered displayed relations are \
explicitly labelled unnumbered.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48cb6d6a-c55a-1140-855d-61ef205f47d6"],

Cell["\<\
1.1 Diagram generation: A-11-01 (Eq. 11.1, p. 93); A-11-02 and A-11-03 \
(momentum-space propagator and quartic vertex, unnumbered, pp. 93\[Dash]94); \
A-11-04 (Gamma(2)=1/W, unnumbered, p. 94); A-11-05 (tadpole and factor 1/2, \
unnumbered, pp. 95\[Dash]96); A-12-01 (four-point bubbles and channel \
permutations, unnumbered, pp. 102\[Dash]104). FeynArts output is a \
software-generated check, not a textbook equation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53c3a23c-1d60-fa4e-a9c9-58d56812b3a4"],

Cell["\<\
1.2 Regularization: A-11-07 (tadpole integral, unnumbered, p. 95); A-12-02 \
(bubble integral, unnumbered, p. 103); A-13-01 (dimensional continuation, \
Section 13, pp. 113\[Dash]114); A-13-02 through A-13-05 (Eqs. \
13.4\[Dash]13.8, pp. 114\[Dash]115); A-13-06 (cutoff-pole comparison, \
discussion following Eq. 13.6, p. 115). Closed cutoff expressions and \
finite-momentum parameter integrals are project derivations from these \
starting integrals.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82f45a22-020b-e245-94c2-7ce9535620d9"],

Cell["\<\
1.3 Counterterms and schemes: A-12-03 and A-12-04 (bare/renormalized action \
and counterterm identities, unnumbered, pp. 106\[Dash]108); A-13-07 (Eqs. \
13.9\[Dash]13.10, p. 117); A-13-08 (Eq. 13.11, p. 118); A-13-09 (Eqs. 13.12\
\[Dash]13.13, p. 119); A-15-01 (MOM conditions Eqs. 15.3\[Dash]15.5, pp. 148\
\[Dash]150); A-15-02 (scheme-coordinate relation, Eq. 15.1, p. 146).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9daafd6c-b67a-0a4e-a77e-28789bcc54f5"],

Cell["\<\
1.4 Beta function and fixed point: A-15-03 through A-15-07 (Eqs. \
15.15\[Dash]15.19, pp. 155\[Dash]156); A-21-01 (Eqs. 21.4\[Dash]21.7, pp. 217\
\[Dash]219); A-21-02 (Wilson\[Dash]Fisher fixed point, Eq. 21.9, p. 220); \
A-21-03 (flow convention, Eqs. 21.10\[Dash]21.13, pp. 220\[Dash]221). Convert \
lambda to g=lambda/(16 Pi^2) explicitly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bc1ea4d-d149-1a45-98a1-a865844e7e7b"],

Cell["\<\
2.1 Sunset: A-12-05 and A-12-06 (sunset topology and symmetry factor 1/3!, \
unnumbered, p. 105); A-12-07 (momentum-dependent subtraction, unnumbered, p. \
106); A-13-10 (DR Gamma-function integral machinery, Eqs. 13.4\[Dash]13.8, \
pp. 114\[Dash]115). The complete massless two-loop convolution is a project \
derivation, not a verbatim FieldsI-Notes equation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25aa8dc1-4123-df4d-b6db-a1f86514e3cf"],

Cell["\<\
2.2 Field renormalization: A-12-08 and A-12-09 (p^2 divergence and \
phi=Z^(-1/2) phi_0, unnumbered, pp. 106\[Dash]108); A-15-08 (Eq. 15.16, p. \
155); A-15-09 (Eq. 15.18, p. 156); A-21-04 (fixed-point field dimension, \
discussion after Eq. 21.14, p. 223).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aa1c6aee-2bcf-a144-91ec-ccdfd3965464"],

Cell["\<\
2.3 Critical isotherm: A-20-01 (critical two-point scaling, unnumbered, p. \
211); A-20-02 (Eqs. 20.2\[Dash]20.5, pp. 211\[Dash]212); A-20-03 \
(delta=(d-D_phi)/D_phi, unnumbered, p. 213); A-20-04 (liquid-gas / Ising \
universality discussion, p. 214); A-21-05 (D_phi at Wilson\[Dash]Fisher fixed \
point, p. 223). A-EXT-01 through A-EXT-04 identify water, bootstrap, \
pressure-density mapping, and scattering as external inputs or project-level \
physical identifications, not textbook-derived numerical data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"89aa725f-b5b6-3e41-8cc1-d46b9486e280"],

Cell["\<\
Anchor convention warning: FieldsI-Notes uses epsilon=4-d and writes the \
Wilsonian flow as d lambda/dl=-beta(lambda). The project uses g=lambda/(16 \
Pi^2), so epsilon=2 epsilon_FC when translating FeynCalc's D=4-2 epsilon_FC. \
Preserve the book's field convention phi=Z^(-1/2) phi_0. See the companion \
anchor_equation_map.md for the full mapping table and detailed qualifications.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1224ad76-4c86-ee46-82eb-4cc65d966901"],

